export const PATCH_NOTES = Object.freeze({ version: "2.1.0", markdown: "# Delve, Die, Repeat 2.1.0\n\n## Headline\nThe dungeon got meaner, and more honest about it. Every roll now reads high-is-good, the difficulty has gone up, one-blow tricks are once per fight, and you can report a bug or read these notes without leaving the game.\n- Every die roll is roll-high: a bigger number always helps you.\n- The difficulty has gone up.\n- A fight or a store survives a force-close.\n- New in the ☰ menu: REPORT A BUG and PATCH NOTES.\n\n## Classes\n### Fighter\n- Kata: always hit → rolls to hit with three extra winning faces, and still adds your level in damage.\n- Sweep: worked on a lone foe → needs two or more foes (trying it on one costs no turn).\n### Thief\n- Flee bonus: +5 → +3.\n- Feint: always hit → rolls to hit with three extra winning faces, and still adds your level in damage.\n### Acrobat (Thief)\n- Foes hit you on their top 3 faces → their top 4.\n### Pilfer (Thief)\n- Magic items: healing items only → any magic item works, but every use rolls a d20; on a 1 it fails, bursts for d10 damage and turns to dust.\n### Magic User\n- Spell damage: dice × a level multiplier → dice + your level², the same bonus a weapon gets. Fireballs add it once per foe; Acid and Ice add it to the first tick.\n- Magic staff: usable from the bag → an equippable melee weapon (d8) whose power works only while you wield it.\n### Summoner (Magic User)\n- Offence spells: locked at level 1 → open to cast. New weakness: heals you cast restore half.\n\n## Races\n- Size: cosmetic → it matters. Elven and Dwarven heroes are Small, Trolls are Large, everyone else is Human-size. Size changes the damage you deal and how easily you are hit, and the Gauntlet of the Giant and Enlarge each step you up one size.\n\n## Abilities & spells\n- One-blow strikes (Kata, Feint, Death Touch, Silent Step, Overhead Blow, Last Stand): every round → once per fight.\n- Spells cast at foes: some could not be resisted → every one can be, on a d20 where the foe wins on half its intelligence in faces. A resisted spell does nothing, and the Oracle shows the roll.\n- Your own resistance to foe spells: only with intelligence 12+ (85% at 18) → the same half-intelligence scale as foes (5% at 1–2, 45% at 18, 50% at 20).\n- Joiners: never resisted foe spells → resist on the same scale.\n- Freeze: could kill outright → deals d6 + your level², then holds a survivor for d4 rounds. A resist keeps the damage but drops the hold.\n- Timed abilities (Smoke, Sidestep, Battle Roar, Riposte): ran out a round early, so Smoke showed 1 round → last their full stated rounds.\n- Bubble: a bigger Shield → bounces the next blow back at whoever threw it, then a 25 hp film for the rest of that round.\n- Scrolls: Magic Users only → anyone can try. Magic Users and Runes/Signs readers always succeed; everyone else rolls intelligence, and a failure can backfire.\n- Sense Presence: → you win initiative outright and can land critical hits in the dark.\n- Spell books: refilled on any new day → refill only when the party eats.\n- Control spells (Freeze, Stone, Doze, Weaken and the like): held deep foes as well as shallow ones → from floor 12 foes increasingly shake them off.\n\n## Items & gear\n- Cloak of Strength: blocked your own critical hits (a bug) → stops foes' critical hits on you, with a Crit-proof chip while it works.\n- Table-4 +HP dots: multiplied your max HP ×1.6 per pull → a flat raise that never compounds.\n- Wilmst caches: could buy out the store → pay about 100 × the floor depth.\n- Destroyed armour: vanished silently on a swap → the Oracle tells you it was destroyed.\n- Combat ITEMS list: → equipped gear is marked EQUIPPED, and worn-only gear in your bag is greyed out with the reason.\n\n## Monsters & difficulty\n- The difficulty has gone up.\n- Stairs: healed you on the way down → no longer heal.\n- A failed climb or leap: could cost 0 HP → always costs at least 1.\n\n## Interface\n- Every roll you see: mixed directions → high-is-good, with signed modifiers where +2 always helps and −2 always hurts.\n- Walls and crevices: rolled the moment you stepped → a card first: CLIMB IT or LEAP IT, USE LADDER or USE ROPE when you carry one, or TURN BACK for free.\n- Force-closing mid-fight or in a store: escaped it → you come back to the same fight or the same store.\n- Darkness: what you see and what you reveal disagreed → one rule; a torch, the Amulet or Night Vision widens both. Map the Floor lasts until you move.\n- Dying: → the death card stays up full screen, and you can open a read-only final character sheet.\n- Movement: tap only → Settings adds an optional arrow pad, bottom-left or bottom-right.\n- The Oracle: combat lines in the order they happened, and every line says what happened, to whom and why.\n- Fights show every active effect on you and on the foe it touches.\n- Acute Hearing: → hears the next room, marking something unseen within 3 squares.\n- Leaderboards: ME | ALL | FRIENDS scopes; your own score is tagged YOU; LINEAGE and GRAVEYARD are your personal boards; LEANEST is gone.\n- The rail card now shows over the store, loot and stair screens, with their buttons hidden until you dismiss it. The find card scrolls, with its rows kept apart.\n- Music: twice as loud by default (turn it down in Settings).\n- The ☰ menu gains REPORT A BUG (sends what you type and this run's Oracle to the developer, posted publicly on GitHub) and PATCH NOTES (these notes, even offline).\n\n## Bug fixes\n- Traps: could kill you while the Oracle said −1 HP → the HP shown is the HP taken.\n- A wandering monster interrupting your step onto a dot, trap or chest: left it unresolved → it resolves after the fight.\n- Ailment rolls of 5–6: announced a disease you never got → name the phobia you do get.\n- Reading a scroll in combat: narrated a level refusal → casts cleanly.\n- The oldest row of THE FIGHT SO FAR: could not be tapped → reveals its roll like the others.\n- Your own leaderboard score: tagged FRIEND → tagged YOU, and every finished run now reaches every board it qualifies for.\n" });
